```sql
SELECT '__BOURBON_WHISKY_FOUR_ROSES_4_CL__', lowest_price FROM table_name
UNION ALL
SELECT '__BOURBON_WHISKY_FOUR_ROSES_4_CL__', LOWER(LOWEST_PRICE) + 1 AS lowest_price FROM table_name
UNION ALL
... (Repeat the same process for each dish with varying prices)
```

After executing this operation, you will have multiple rows for each dish with different prices. Then, you can use the AVG function to find the average price of each dish:

```sql
SELECT name, AVG(lowest_price) as avg_price FROM (
    SELECT '__BOURBON_WHISKY_FOUR_ROSES_4_CL__' as name, lowest_price FROM table_name
    UNION ALL
    SELECT '__BOURBON_WHISKY_FOUR_ROSES_4_CL__', LOWER(LOWEST_PRICE) + 1 AS lowest_price FROM table_name
    ... (Repeat the same process for each dish)
) as combined_table GROUP BY name;
```

This will give you the average price of each dish in the table.
